---
/**
 * Terms of Service — Brick Crack (App Store) / Brick Game (Google Play)
 *
 * Standalone page for the store listings, same layout as /brickcrack-privacy.
 * Not linked from the site nav. /brickgame-terms redirects here
 * (public/brickgame-terms/index.html). TR mirror at /tr/brickcrack-terms so the
 * header's language toggle doesn't 404.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { type Lang } from '@lib/i18n';

const lang: Lang = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Terms of Service — Brick Crack (Brick Game)"
  description="Terms of Service for Brick Crack (App Store) / Brick Game (Google Play), the mobile block puzzle by Ekimoz Games."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <header class="mb-10 border-b border-border pb-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display font-medium text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-100 tracking-tight"
      >
        Terms of Service — Brick Crack (Brick Game)
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-text-200 leading-relaxed">
        Developer: Ekimoz Games (Yusuf Kaan Usta), Türkiye<br />
        Contact: <a class="text-accent-2 hover:underline underline-offset-4" href="mailto:kaanekimoz@gmail.com">kaanekimoz@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-300 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">
        Effective date: November 18, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-content space-y-4 text-text-200 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the mobile game
        <strong>Brick Crack</strong>, published as <em>Brick Game</em> on Google
        Play ("the Game"), made by Ekimoz Games (Yusuf Kaan Usta, "we", "us").
        How the Game handles information is described in the
        <a href="/brickcrack-privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Acceptance and scope</h2>
      <p>
        By downloading, installing or playing the Game you agree to these Terms. If
        you do not agree, do not use the Game.
      </p>
      <p>
        "Brick Crack" on the App Store and "Brick Game" on Google Play are the same
        game (package / bundle ID <code>com.ekimozgames.brickgame</code> on both),
        and these Terms cover both versions. They apply in addition to the terms of
        the store you got the Game from (the App Store or Google Play).
      </p>

      <h2>2. License to use the Game</h2>
      <p>
        We grant you a limited, personal, non-commercial, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable and revocable license to install and play the Game on
        devices you own or control. You may not sell, rent, sublicense or otherwise
        transfer the Game or this license.
      </p>

      <h2>3. In-app purchases</h2>
      <p>The Game offers two optional in-app purchases:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Premium</strong> unlocks levels 16–115 and all themes, and removes
          ads.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Remove Ads</strong> removes ads.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Both are one-time purchases (non-consumable): you pay once and keep them.
        Payment is handled by Google Play Billing on Android and Apple In-App
        Purchase on iOS. We never receive your card details; the Game only sees
        the store's confirmation that a purchase was made.
      </p>
      <p>
        Purchases stay linked to your store account. If you reinstall the Game or
        move to a new device, use <strong>Restore Purchases</strong>, which you can
        find in the Premium panel and in the pause menu. Refunds are handled by
        Google Play or Apple under their own refund policies; we cannot issue them
        ourselves.
      </p>

      <h2>4. In-game progress and content</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Unlocked levels, themes, scores and other in-game progress have
          <strong>no real-money value</strong>. They cannot be exchanged for cash,
          sold, or transferred to another person.
        </li>
        <li>
          Levels, themes and other content may change as the Game is updated.
        </li>
        <li>
          Progress is stored on your device. If the Game's data on your device is
          deleted (for example by uninstalling the Game), that progress is lost and
          we cannot restore it. On Android, the parts saved to Google Play Games
          cloud save are described in the
          <a href="/brickcrack-privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Purchases can always
          be brought back with Restore Purchases.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The Game shows ads (banner, interstitial and optional rewarded ads) through
        Unity LevelPlay (ironSource) and Unity Ads. Ads are not personalized. We
        are not responsible for the content of third-party ads or for the products
        and services they promote. See the
        <a href="/brickcrack-privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how ad data is handled.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Google Play Games features (Android only)</h2>
      <p>
        On Android, the Game uses Google Play Games Services for sign-in,
        leaderboards, achievements and cloud save. When you use these features,
        Google's own terms and privacy policy also apply. These features are not
        available in the iOS version.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Unacceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          cheat, or use bots, scripts or other tools that give you an unfair
          advantage;
        </li>
        <li>
          modify, hack or tamper with the Game, its files or its saved data;
        </li>
        <li>
          reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Game, except where the law
          expressly allows it;
        </li>
        <li>
          manipulate leaderboards or achievements, for example by submitting scores
          you did not legitimately earn;
        </li>
        <li>use the Game in any way that breaks the law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Game, including its design, artwork, sound and code, belongs to Ekimoz
        Games. These Terms do not give you any ownership of it. You may not copy or
        redistribute any part of the Game except as allowed by law.
      </p>

      <h2>9. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The Game is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
        kind, express or implied. We do not guarantee that the Game will be free
        of errors or interruptions, or that it will run on every device.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for
        any indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for any loss of data
        or in-game progress, arising from your use of or inability to use the Game.
        Nothing in these Terms limits any rights you have as a consumer that cannot
        be limited under applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms when the Game changes. The effective date at the
        top of this page shows the latest version. If you keep using the Game after
        an update, you accept the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using the Game at any time by uninstalling it. Your license
        ends automatically if you break these Terms. We may also discontinue the
        Game or remove it from the stores.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Türkiye.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact</h2>
      <p>For questions about these Terms or about the Game, please write to:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Yusuf Kaan Usta</strong> (Ekimoz Games)<br />
        <a href="mailto:kaanekimoz@gmail.com">kaanekimoz@gmail.com</a><br />
        Türkiye
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
